The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
rstc = devm_reset_control_array_get(&pdev->dev, false, false);
if (IS_ERR(rstc)) {
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
}
```
Reason:
The unconditional printing of the error message when `devm_reset_control_array_get` fails does not differentiate between a genuine error and a probe deferral scenario. This can mislead users into thinking there is a critical failure when, in fact, probe deferral is a normal part of device initialization.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (PTR_ERR(rstc) != -EPROBE_DEFER)
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
```
Reason:
This modification checks if the error returned by `devm_reset_control_array_get` is specifically a probe deferral error (`-EPROBE_DEFER`). If it is, the error message is not printed, thus preventing misleading information from being presented to the user during normal device initialization.

